@issue-321 @execute @checkpoint @cross-platform
Feature: Migrate completed legacy execute checkpoints before identity enforcement
  As a maintainer executing an approved issue after upgrading nmg-sdlc
  I want fully completed pre-identity checkpoints released through guarded cleanup
  So that obsolete terminal runtime cannot block a fresh queue or weaken identity safety

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Completed released legacy checkpoint is migrated before identity enforcement
    Given schema-version-1 run.json contains the exact fully completed issue-6 legacy payload with no identity fields
    And exact issue-6 handoffs, worker provenance, a checkpoint temporary file, and unrelated runtime exist
    When the execute controller starts approved eligible issue 19
    Then only the issue-6 owned handoffs, worker provenance, temporary file, and checkpoint are released
    And unrelated runtime remains
    And issue 19 starts without "Run checkpoint identity mismatch"
    And its checkpoint has a new complete identity, native canonical project root, and positive revision

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unsafe legacy candidates remain identity mismatches
    Given the issue-6 checkpoint is <state>
    When the execute controller requests issue 19
    Then it exits status 1 with stderr exactly "Run checkpoint identity mismatch"
    And the checkpoint bytes and supporting runtime are unchanged
    And no issue-19 worker starts

    Examples:
      | state |
      | incomplete |
      | active |
      | failed |
      | remediating |
      | malformed |
      | missing terminal completion evidence |
      | one of all 62 non-empty proper identity-field subsets |
      | a complete but invalid identity |

  @SCN003 @regression @safety
  Scenario Outline: Cleanup and identity hazards fail before fresh-run creation
    Given a fully completed legacy checkpoint encounters <hazard>
    When the execute controller requests issue 19
    Then migration fails closed without starting or advancing issue 19
    And runtime outside exact owned artifacts is not removed
    And identity-bound CAS and exact-head checks remain enforced

    Examples:
      | hazard |
      | a held checkpoint lock |
      | an exact owned artifact deletion failure |
      | checkpoint bytes changed after classification |
      | a foreign or changed controller lease |
      | a stale identity-bound revision |
      | identity-bound branch or head drift |

  @SCN004 @regression @cross-platform
  Scenario Outline: Logical checkpoint classification is host-independent
    Given deterministic checkpoint bytes use <newline> serialization
    And identity path values, when present, use <path-form> syntax
    When the fully unbound payload and every partial-identity payload are classified
    Then the fully unbound terminal payload is migratable on every host
    And every partial-identity payload is rejected on every host
    And native cleanup creates issue 19 with projectRoot equal to the temporary root realpath

    Examples:
      | newline | path-form |
      | LF | POSIX |
      | LF | Windows |
      | CRLF | POSIX |
      | CRLF | Windows |

  @SCN005 @regression @safety @cross-platform
  Scenario Outline: Native link and ownership boundaries remain fail-closed
    Given legacy cleanup reaches <native-boundary>
    When cleanup runs on the applicable native CI host
    Then it does not escape the canonical project runtime
    And it does not delete foreign runtime or another controller's lease
    And the prior checkpoint remains diagnosable unless an exact owned artifact was already removed

    Examples:
      | native-boundary |
      | a POSIX directory symbolic link |
      | a Windows directory junction |
      | a permitted Windows directory symbolic link |
      | a held checkpoint lock |
      | changed checkpoint bytes |
      | a foreign or changed controller lease |
